# The Docker Engine apt repository, in deb822 format.
#
# Vendored rather than written by install.sh with a heredoc, for the same
# reason starship.toml and mise/config.toml are files instead of generated
# text: this repo declares artefacts, it does not fabricate them. What apt
# trusts is reviewable in a diff here, not assembled at runtime on the machine.
#
# Suites is the Ubuntu codename and is pinned rather than resolved from
# /etc/os-release. Resolving it would make a release upgrade silent -- the
# installer would quietly point at a suite Docker may not publish yet, and the
# first sign would be an install that fails on a machine being rebuilt.
# Pinning turns that into an edit somebody has to make and review. Confirmed
# present before pinning: download.docker.com/linux/ubuntu/dists/resolute/
# Release returns 200.
#
# Architectures is likewise explicit. Left off, apt uses whatever the host
# reports; naming it means a diff appears the day this repo is applied to a
# machine that is not amd64, rather than an install that silently pulls
# nothing.
#
# Signed-By points at the key this repo vendors beside this file. That path is
# where wsl/install.sh copies wsl/apt/docker.asc to -- the two must be changed
# together.
Types: deb
URIs: https://download.docker.com/linux/ubuntu
Suites: resolute
Components: stable
Architectures: amd64
Signed-By: /etc/apt/keyrings/docker.asc
